% =====================================================================
% kernel.clausal -- the RESULT-SHAPE vocabulary for eu/procurement/time_limits.
%
% Determination-slices layout (2026-08-07; was schema.clausal). This file
% holds the ONE compound constructor that describes the SHAPE of this
% domain's verdict, and nothing else. No rules, no facts, no imports: it is
% vocabulary, so the shape of an answer does not live inside the slice that
% happens to compute it today.
%
%   time_limits_verdict(STATUS, MINIMUM_DAYS, CONFORMITY, CITATIONS)
%     STATUS in { minimum_days_prescribed, no_minimum_prescribed,
%                 stage_not_applicable }
%     MINIMUM_DAYS: integer day count when minimum_days_prescribed,
%                   the atom n_a otherwise (IC-11 numeric n_a idiom).
%     CONFORMITY in { meets_prescribed_minimum,
%                     shorter_than_prescribed_minimum,
%                     observed_days_not_supplied,
%                     no_prescribed_minimum_to_meet }
%
% THE CONFORMITY SLOT (added 2026-08-23). Arts 27-31 fix a MINIMUM; a record
% shows a limit the notice actually allowed. Comparing the two is arithmetic
% over the statute's own figures with no view about what the record shows, so
% it is the domain's work, not a reviewer's overlay (assess spec §3.1). The
% slot is the answer to "and did they allow that long?", and it is a fourth
% slot rather than a second STATUS vocabulary because the two questions are
% independent: `minimum_days_prescribed` says the Directive fixes a figure,
% CONFORMITY says whether the observed figure clears it.
%
% WHY IT IS NEVER SILENT. There is no value meaning "no comparison happened".
% A prescribed minimum with the observed days unsupplied is
% `observed_days_not_supplied` -- explicitly not a conformity claim -- and the
% two statuses that prescribe no figure at all carry
% `no_prescribed_minimum_to_meet`, the n_a of this slot. Every verdict says
% what it knows about conformity, including that it knows nothing.
%
% WHY IT IS HERE despite this domain having exactly ONE determination slice
% (time_limits.clausal). The recipe's "used by >= 2 slices" bar governs VALUE
% ATOMS; RESULT-SHAPE CONSTRUCTORS are an unconditional kernel category
% regardless of slice count -- see
% `docs/superpowers/plans/recipe-determination-slices-agent-brief.md`,
% "Kernel membership when there is only ONE slice", and the executed
% precedents us/irc_s121 (s121_eligibility), eu/procurement/thresholds
% (threshold_verdict), eu/peppol_einvoicing (peppol_result) and
% eu/gpsr (gpsr_verdict).
%
% Measured here rather than inherited: time_limits_verdict is spelled OUTSIDE
% time_limits.clausal -- in tests/test_load.clausal, tests/test_output_mode.clausal,
% tests/test_properties.clausal and tests/test_public_interface.clausal, and it
% is the term the Python oracle (eval/score_harness.py:126) builds and passes
% as the second argument of decide_time_limits/2. Those consumers ask about the
% SHAPE of the answer without needing the rules that produce it; that is the
% coupling the kernel absorbs.
%
% WHAT LEFT THIS FILE, and why. The old schema.clausal also held the three
% status atoms, the n_a day-slot marker, the overall checklist-row id, the
% five profile-key atoms, the two stage atoms and the four reduction-condition
% atoms. Those are VALUE atoms with exactly ONE slice-level reader
% (time_limits.clausal), so they are now declared there and imported FROM it
% by the top-layer consumers (queries/fixtures) and by the tests. Kernel is
% for slice<->slice sharing only.
%
% The two OTHER shared vocabularies this domain uses are not kernel material
% either: cite/1 + eu_dir_2014_24_art_27..31 are owned by citations.clausal
% (a genuinely horizontal module this refactor does not touch), and item/3
% is the kit's, from formalize_lib. The five procedure atoms
% (open_procedure ...) are owned by eu.procurement.directive_2014_24.vocabulary, shared by six
% domains, and are not this domain's to place.
% =====================================================================

% Clausal Prolog: time_limits_verdict/4 is a data constructor, not a predicate, so
% it is not in the export list (a .clausal module exports predicates only, and a
% compound term needs no import).
:- module(kernel, []).

:- end_module(kernel).
